## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical security design for shared edge environments with tenant isolation, policy distribution, and runtime attestation.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation and WASM sandboxing
- Hardware-backed attestation (TPM/SGX)
- SBOM verification and delta policy updates
- Key management in HSMs and rotation strategies
- Revocation and rollback workflows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: verifyPolicy and attestation check
async function loadPolicy(node, policyPackage) {
  const {sig, hash} = policyPackage;
  if (!verifySig(hash, sig, node.publicKey)) throw new Error('Invalid policy');
  if (!await attestationCheck(node)) throw new Error('Untrusted node');
  // apply policy
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test revocation paths for long-lived sessions?
- What are the trade-offs between delta updates and full policy refresh in terms of latency and risk?

Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design secure multi-tenant serverless with real-world constraints: isolation, attestation, key management, deployment safety, and auditability.

Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation and sandboxing
- Hardware-backed signing (HSM) and per-tenant keys
- Runtime attestation and manifest/SBOM checks
- Ephemeral credentials and mTLS
- Canary deployments, rollback, tamper-evident logs
- Key rotation and incident response

Code Example

```javascript
// Example: verify signed package manifest before deployment
const crypto = require('crypto');
const manifest = loadManifest(tenantId);
const signatureBase64 = loadSignature(tenantId);
const publicKeyPem = loadPublicKey(tenantId);

const verifier = crypto.createVerify('SHA256');
verifier.update(manifest);
verifier.end();
const ok = verifier.verify(publicKeyPem, signatureBase64, 'base64');
```

